    FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
    AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
    LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
    FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
    DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

Only the palette values and their backstories are taken. None of the `ltc`
package's functions are included: vellum's own colour engine, CVD simulation
and audit are used instead.

Two of the thirty-two are not original to `ltc` and are noted as such in the
catalogue: `heatmap2` and `heatmap3` are ColorBrewer's RdBu 5-class and RdYlBu
5-class schemes, by Cynthia Brewer, Mark Harrower and The Pennsylvania State
University (https://colorbrewer2.org), which are licensed under the Apache
License 2.0. A third, `trio3`, is the first three Okabe-Ito colours.


2. Paul Tol's colour schemes  (R/palettes.R)
--------------------------------------------

The `tol` palette family is transcribed from Paul Tol's SRON technical note
(https://sronpersonalpages.nl/~pault/), which places the schemes in the public
domain for free use.


3. Okabe-Ito  (R/palettes.R)
----------------------------

The Okabe-Ito colour-universal-design palette is published by Masataka Okabe
and Kei Ito at https://jfly.uni-koeln.de/color/ for free use with attribution.
